<header class="sg-head"><p class="featured-region">Anthem · Celebration · 1785 · Europe</p><h1 class="sg-title">Ode to Joy</h1><p class="sg-local"><bdi lang="de">An die Freude</bdi></p><p class="sg-kid" data-say>A poem about joy and friendship from 1785 that Beethoven set to music in his Ninth Symphony; its tune is now the anthem of Europe.</p></header>
<dl class="sg-facts"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd>Friedrich Schiller</dd></div><div><dt>Music</dt><dd>Ludwig van Beethoven</dd></div><div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>German poetry and music of the late Enlightenment; later Europe as a whole</dd></div><div><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd></div><div><dt>Place</dt><dd>Gohlis, Leipzig, Germany</dd></div><div><dt>Date</dt><dd>poem written in the summer of 1785; Beethoven's setting in the Ninth Symphony completed in 1824</dd></div><div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Anthem · Celebration</dd></div><div><dt>The words</dt><dd>Public domain (words by Friedrich Schiller (written 1785, published 1786; he died in 1805))</dd></div></dl>
<div class="sg-body">
<section class="sg-sec" id="story"><h2>The story</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-schiller">Friedrich Schiller</a> wrote &quot;An die Freude&quot; in the summer of 1785. From the beginning of May until mid-September that year he stayed with his publisher, Georg Joachim Göschen, at Gohlis near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, where he wrote the poem together with his play Don Carlos. The friendship of Christian Gottfried Körner, his longtime friend and patron, had inspired it. The ode was published the next year in the magazine Thalia. A slightly revised version, which changed two lines of the first stanza and left out the last stanza, was published after Schiller's death, in 1808. Schiller himself later judged the poem a failure: in an 1800 letter to Körner he called it &quot;detached from reality&quot;.</p><p>Some writers have speculated that Schiller first wrote an &quot;Ode to Freedom&quot; and changed it to &quot;To Joy&quot;; Beethoven's biographer Alexander Wheelock Thayer suggested this. The musicologist Alexander Rehding notes that scholarly consensus finds no factual basis for the idea, and that even <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonard-bernstein">Leonard Bernstein</a>, who used &quot;Freiheit&quot; in two performances in 1989, called it conjecture.</p><p>The poem is best known through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-van-beethoven">Ludwig van Beethoven</a>, who used the 1808 version in the final, fourth movement of his Ninth Symphony, completed in 1824. Beethoven's text does not follow Schiller's poem entirely and adds some new sections. Other composers had set the poem before him, among them Körner himself (1786), Carl Friedrich Zelter (1792) and Johann Friedrich Reichardt (1796), and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-schubert">Franz Schubert</a> (1815) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-ilyich-tchaikovsky">Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky</a> (1865).</p><p>Beethoven's melody, without Schiller's words, was adopted as the anthem of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-europe">Council of Europe</a> in 1972 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> in 1985, known as the Anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The same melody served as the national anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ian-smith">Ian Smith</a>'s Rhodesia from 1974 to 1979, as &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rise-o-voices-of-rhodesia">Rise, O Voices of Rhodesia</a>&quot;.</p><p>The setting has also been sung in protest and remembrance. In 1957 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-robeson">Paul Robeson</a>, blacklisted and with his passport revoked, sang it to a festival of 5,000 miners in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> over a transatlantic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telephone">telephone</a> line. Under the military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> in Chile (1973–1990), women gathered outside prisons to sing a Spanish version, &quot;Himno a la Alegría&quot;, to bring hope to those held inside. Chinese students broadcast it during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre">Tiananmen Square protests</a> of 1989, and on Christmas Day 1989, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-the-berlin-wall">fall of the Berlin Wall</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonard-bernstein">Leonard Bernstein</a> conducted it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> with choir and orchestra members from East and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yiddish">Yiddish</a> version by Isaac Leib Peretz from the 1890s is still used as a Jewish protest song.</p><p>Today it is performed at Daiku (&quot;Number Nine&quot;) concerts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> every December, was played after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emmanuel-macron">Emmanuel Macron</a>'s victory in the French presidential election of 2017, and, as an instrumental, serves as the anthem of UEFA's European Qualifiers and of the Copa Libertadores.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="meaning"><h2>What it says</h2><p>A hymn in which joy is pictured as a divine spark that draws all people together as brothers. It celebrates friendship and love and looks upward to a creator above the stars, in a mood of exalted, communal celebration.</p></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="words"><h2>The words</h2><div class="sg-show" role="group" aria-label="Show these columns"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="orig">German</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-col="en">In English</button></div><div class="sg-blocks"><div class="sg-lyrics sg-cols-2"><div class="sg-colhead" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sg-o">German</span><span class="sg-e">In English</span></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Freude, schöner Götterfunken,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Joy, beautiful spark of the gods,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Tochter aus Elisium,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>daughter from Elysium,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Wir betreten feuertrunken</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>we enter, drunk with fire,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Himmlische, dein Heiligthum.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>heavenly one, your sanctuary.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Deine Zauber binden wieder,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Your magic binds again</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">was der Mode Schwerd getheilt;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>what the sword of fashion divided;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Bettler werden Fürstenbrüder,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>beggars become brothers of princes</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">wo dein sanfter Flügel weilt.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>where your gentle wing lingers.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Seid umschlungen, Millionen!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Be embraced, millions!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Diesen Kuß der ganzen Welt!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>This kiss to the whole world!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Brüder – überm Sternenzelt</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Brothers – above the tent of stars</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">muß ein lieber Vater wohnen.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>a loving father must dwell.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Wem der große Wurf gelungen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Whoever has succeeded in the great throw</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">eines Freundes Freund zu seyn;</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>of being a friend's friend;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">wer ein holdes Weib errungen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>whoever has won a lovely wife,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">mische seinen Jubel ein!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>let him mix in his rejoicing!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Ja – wer auch nur eine Seele</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Yes – whoever calls even one soul</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">sein nennt auf dem Erdenrund!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>his own on the round of the earth!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Und wer’s nie gekonnt, der stehle</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>And whoever never could, let him steal</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">weinend sich aus diesem Bund!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>away weeping from this league!</span></p></div><details class="sg-more"><summary>Show all 108 lines</summary><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Was den großen Ring bewohnet</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Whatever dwells in the great ring,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">huldige der Simpathie!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>let it pay homage to sympathy!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Zu den Sternen leitet sie,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To the stars she leads,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Wo der Unbekannte tronet.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>where the Unknown One is enthroned.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Freude trinken alle Wesen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>All beings drink joy</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">an den Brüsten der Natur,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>at the breasts of nature;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Alle Guten, alle Bösen</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>all the good, all the wicked</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">folgen ihrer Rosenspur.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>follow her trail of roses.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Küße gab sie uns und Reben,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Kisses she gave us, and vines,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">einen Freund, geprüft im Tod.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>a friend, proven in death.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Wollust ward dem Wurm gegeben,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Sensual pleasure was given to the worm,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">und der Cherub steht vor Gott.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and the cherub stands before God.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Ihr stürzt nieder, Millionen?</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>You fall down, millions?</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Ahndest du den Schöpfer, Welt?</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Do you sense the Creator, world?</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Such’ ihn überm Sternenzelt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Seek him above the tent of stars;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">über Sternen muß er wohnen.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>above the stars he must dwell.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Freude heißt die starke Feder</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Joy is the name of the strong spring</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">in der ewigen Natur.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in eternal nature.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Freude, Freude treibt die Räder</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Joy, joy drives the wheels</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">in der großen Weltenuhr.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in the great clock of the worlds.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Blumen lockt sie aus den Keimen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>She lures flowers out of the seeds,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Sonnen aus dem Firmament,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>suns out of the firmament,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Sphären rollt sie in den Räumen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>she rolls spheres in the spaces</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">die des Sehers Rohr nicht kennt!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>that the seer's tube does not know!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Froh, wie seine Sonnen fliegen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Glad, as his suns fly</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">durch des Himmels prächtgen Plan,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>through the splendid plain of heaven,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Laufet Brüder eure Bahn,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>run your course, brothers,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">freudig wie ein Held zum siegen.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>joyful as a hero to victory.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Aus der Wahrheit Feuerspiegel</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>From the fiery mirror of truth</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">lächelt sie den Forscher an.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>she smiles at the seeker.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Zu der Tugend steilem Hügel</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>To the steep hill of virtue</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">leitet sie des Dulders Bahn.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>she guides the sufferer's path.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Auf des Glaubens Sonnenberge</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>On the sunlit mountain of faith</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">sieht man ihre Fahnen wehn,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>one sees her banners wave;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Durch den Riß gesprengter Särge</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>through the crack of burst coffins</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">sie im Chor der Engel stehn.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>one sees her stand in the choir of angels.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Duldet mutig, Millionen!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Endure bravely, millions!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Duldet für die beßre Welt!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Endure for the better world!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Droben überm Sternenzelt</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Up there above the tent of stars</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">wird ein großer Gott belohnen.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>a great God will reward.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Göttern kann man nicht vergelten,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Gods cannot be repaid;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">schön ists ihnen gleich zu seyn.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>it is beautiful to be like them.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Gram und Armut soll sich melden</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Grief and poverty, let them come forward</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">mit den Frohen sich erfreun.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>to rejoice with the joyful.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Groll und Rache sei vergessen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Let grudge and revenge be forgotten,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">unserm Todfeind sei verziehn.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>our mortal enemy be forgiven.</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Keine Thräne soll ihn pressen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>No tear shall press him,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">keine Reue nage ihn.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>no remorse gnaw at him.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Unser Schuldbuch sei vernichtet!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Let our book of debts be destroyed!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">ausgesöhnt die ganze Welt!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>the whole world reconciled!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Brüder – überm Sternenzelt</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Brothers – above the tent of stars</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">richtet Gott wie wir gerichtet.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>God judges as we have judged.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Freude sprudelt in Pokalen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Joy bubbles in goblets;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">in der Traube goldnem Blut</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>in the golden blood of the grape</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">trinken Sanftmut Kannibalen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>cannibals drink gentleness,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Die Verzweiflung Heldenmut – –</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>despair drinks heroic courage – –</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Brüder fliegt von euren Sitzen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Brothers, fly from your seats</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">wenn der volle Römer kraißt,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>when the full wine-glass goes round;</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Laßt den Schaum zum Himmel sprützen:</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>let the foam spurt up to heaven:</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Dieses Glas dem guten Geist.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>this glass to the good spirit.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Den der Sterne Wirbel loben,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Him whom the whirl of the stars praises,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">den des Seraphs Hymne preist,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>whom the seraph's hymn extols:</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Dieses Glas dem guten Geist,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>this glass to the good spirit</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">überm Sternenzelt dort oben!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>above the tent of stars up there!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Festen Mut in schwerem Leiden,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Firm courage in heavy suffering,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Hülfe, wo die Unschuld weint,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>help where innocence weeps,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Ewigkeit geschwornen Eiden,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>eternity to oaths that are sworn,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Wahrheit gegen Freund und Feind,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>truth towards friend and foe,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Männerstolz vor Königstronen, –</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>manly pride before the thrones of kings, –</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Brüder, gält’ es Gut und Blut –</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>brothers, even if it cost goods and blood –</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Dem Verdienste seine Kronen,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>to merit its crowns,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Untergang der Lügenbrut!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>downfall to the brood of lies!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Schließt den heilgen Zirkel dichter,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Close the holy circle tighter,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">schwört bei diesem goldnen Wein:</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>swear by this golden wine</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Dem Gelübde treu zu sein,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>to be true to the vow,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">schwört es bei dem Sternenrichter!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>swear it by the judge of the stars!</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Rettung von Tirannenketten,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Rescue from tyrants' chains,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Großmut auch dem Bösewicht,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>magnanimity even to the villain,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Hoffnung auf den Sterbebetten,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>hope on the deathbeds,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Gnade auf dem Hochgericht!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>mercy on the scaffold!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Auch die Toden sollen leben!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>The dead too shall live!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Brüder trinkt und stimmet ein,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Brothers, drink and join in:</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Allen Sündern soll vergeben,</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>all sinners shall be forgiven,</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">und die Hölle nicht mehr seyn.</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>and hell shall be no more.</span></p></div><div class="sg-st"><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Eine heitre Abschiedsstunde!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>A cheerful hour of parting!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">süßen Schlaf im Leichentuch!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>sweet sleep in the shroud!</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Brüder – einen sanften Spruch</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>Brothers – a gentle sentence</span></p><p class="sg-ln"><span class="sg-o" lang="de">Aus des Todtenrichters Munde!</span><span class="sg-e" data-say>from the mouth of the judge of the dead!</span></p></div></details></div></div><div class="sg-credit"><p>Original: Friedrich Schiller, An die Freude (1786 printing). Text from <a href="https://de.wikisource.org/wiki/An_die_Freude_(Schiller)" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; public domain.</p><p>The English is the Institute&#8217;s own translation, made from the original for this page.</p></div><details class="sg-notes"><summary>Notes on the translation (17)</summary><ul><li>This is the 1786 text (Thalia), not the 1803 revision Beethoven set in 1824: lines 1.6-1.7 here read 'what the sword of fashion divided; beggars become brothers of princes', where 1803 has 'what fashion strictly divided; all men become brothers'. The 1803 text also drops the last stanza pair (17-18 here). Do not present this translation as the words of Beethoven's Ninth.</li><li>Spelling is the 1786 printing's (Elisium, Heiligthum, Schwerd, seyn, Simpathie, tronet, kraißt, Todten); translated as the modern words.</li><li>Stanzas alternate solo and chorus: the even-numbered four-line stanzas are the chorus ('Chor') of the original printing.</li><li>line 3.1: 'der große Wurf' is literally 'the great throw' (of dice), i.e. the great stroke of fortune; kept literal.</li><li>line 4.1: 'der große Ring' (the great ring) is the round world or the whole of creation.</li><li>line 4.2: 'Simpathie' in the 18th-century sense: the attraction or fellow-feeling that binds all beings, not pity.</li><li>line 5.7: 'Wollust' is sensual pleasure or delight (not only 'lust' in the modern sense).</li><li>line 7.5: 'Keimen' are seeds or germs; 'buds' is also possible.</li><li>line 7.8: 'des Sehers Rohr' is the seer's (astronomer's) tube, i.e. the telescope.</li><li>line 8.2: 'Plan' here is the old sense 'plain, level expanse', not 'design'; 'plan' is possible but less likely.</li><li>line 9.8: the verb 'sieht man' (one sees) carries over from line 9.6; supplied as 'one sees her stand'.</li><li>line 13.4: the verb 'trinken' (drink) carries over from line 13.3; supplied once.</li><li>line 13.6: 'der volle Römer' is a Römer, a large stemmed wine-glass (English 'rummer'); 'kraißt' = 'kreist', goes round.</li><li>line 15.6: 'gält' es Gut und Blut' = 'were it to cost property and life (blood)'.</li><li>line 15.7: 'Dem Verdienste seine Kronen' = to merit (desert) its crowns, i.e. let merit be crowned.</li><li>line 17.4: 'Hochgericht' is the place of execution, the gallows or scaffold.</li><li>line 16.4: 'Sternenrichter' is literally 'star-judge', the judge above (or of) the stars.</li></ul></details></section>
